# TDD Testing

Purpose:
  TDD Testing

Skill: TDD Testing

ID:
  SKILL-CROSS-TEST-TDD

Domain:
  cross-cutting/testing

Use:
  test-driven development

Apply:
  intermediate
  senior
  unit-testing
  code-quality

Requires:
  testing-fundamentals
  xunit-framework

Avoid:
  test-after-development
  testing-implementation
  over-mocking
  test-brittleness

Level:
  L1

Status:
  STABLE

Maturity:
  MATURE

Risk:
  LOW

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  tdd
  test driven development
  red green refactor
  unit test
  xunit

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/testing/tdd.md

Evidence:
  - Test-Driven Development by Kent Beck
  - xUnit Documentation
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [T1] Write test before implementation.
  [T2] Follow Red-Green-Refactor cycle.
  [T3] Write minimal test to fail.
  [T4] Write minimal code to pass.
  [T5] Refactor after green.
  [T6] Tests MUST be independent.
  [T7] Tests MUST be fast.
  [T8] Tests MUST be repeatable.

Pros:
  - Better design
  - Regression prevention
  - Living documentation

Cons:
  - Slow initial development
  - Requires discipline
  - Hard to learn

Alternatives:
  - BDD
  - Property-based testing
  - Integration testing

State: +

